# Soft admin detail sections

Soft **entity overview** pages of the same nature (Organization, Branch, Court, pricing profile) share **one section-gap / column convention**. Do not invent a second gap, column width, or panel pad per entity.

## Tokens (required)

From [`apps/admin-web/components/data-list/index.ts`](apps/admin-web/components/data-list/index.ts):

| Token | Role |
| --- | --- |
| `softContentMaxW` | Content column (`max-w-5xl`) |
| `softDetailSectionGap` | Vertical gap hero ↔ panels and panel ↔ panel / grid |

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — ad-hoc spacing / width
<div className="px-4 pt-1">
  <Hero />
  <div className="space-y-3 max-w-6xl">…</div>
</div>

// ✅ GOOD — Soft entity overview stack
<div
  className={cn(
    "mx-auto flex w-full flex-col px-4 pb-6 pt-3 md:px-5 md:pt-4",
    softContentMaxW,
    softDetailSectionGap,
  )}
>
  <SoftHero /> {/* card only — soft-elevated rounded-3xl, no outer page pad */}
  <EntityDetailPanel title=… hint=…>…</EntityDetailPanel>
  <div className={cn("grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-2", softDetailSectionGap)}>
    <EntityDetailPanel>…</EntityDetailPanel>
    <EntityDetailPanel>…</EntityDetailPanel>
  </div>
</div>
```

If a parent layout already wraps children in `softContentMaxW`, the overview stack may omit a second `softContentMaxW` but **must** still use `softDetailSectionGap` (and the same page pad when the layout does not already pad).

## Soft cover hero (overview only)

Org / Branch (and Profile / User when they use Soft cover) use Soft cover + logo overlap on the **overview** tab only. Court overview may use a title-row + panels without Soft cover — still use `softDetailSectionGap` between sections.

## Secondary detail tabs

Tabs that are not Soft-cover overview (schedule, holidays, images, amenities, courts list, pricing list, user sessions/security, org holidays, …) still use `softDetailSectionGap` between `EntityDetailPanel` blocks / major sections.

- Prefer shared wrappers: Branch → `BranchTabBody` (already applies the token).
- Organization sections (branches, courts, team, holidays, bookings) use `OrganizationSectionFrame`: title row, optional toolbar, scrolling body. The body is a card grid, a list/table, or panels. Do not add a Soft cover hero, and do not wrap the section in a second full-height card.
- Branches and courts are the two sections that switch between grid and list. The choice is stored per signed-in user (`bokdy.admin.collectionView.${userId}.branches` / `.courts`).
- Soft cover hero is **not** required on secondary tabs.
- Do not redesign list/table chrome; only unify section stack gap.

```tsx
// ❌ BAD
<div className="flex flex-col gap-3 p-5">…</div>
<div className="flex flex-col gap-4 p-5 pt-2 md:gap-5">…</div>

// ✅ GOOD
<div className={cn("flex flex-col p-5 pt-2 md:px-6", softDetailSectionGap)}>…</div>
```

## Rules

1. **Same-nature = same stack** — Org / Branch / Court overview (+ pricing detail panel stacks) must share `softDetailSectionGap` and default `EntityDetailPanel` padding (`p-5`). Do not ship `pt-1` under a Soft hero or one-off `gap-3` / `p-4` overrides that drift from peers.
2. **Hero is overview-only** — Soft cover + logo overlap lives on the overview tab; other tabs do not repeat the avatar/banner hero.
3. **Panels** — Use `EntityDetailPanel` with section `hint` when the section needs an InfoHint. Always show important fields empty as `—` (see `frontend-detail-fields-visible`).
4. **Profile rows** — Prefer fixed-width label left + value (`w-28` label pattern) on Soft entity overviews. Do not mix `justify-between` and fixed-label rows across the same entity family without reason.
5. **No hardcoding** — Do not hardcode `max-w-5xl`, `max-w-6xl`, or one-off `gap-3`/`pt-1`/`gap-4 md:gap-5` between Soft detail sections; use the tokens.

## Golden paths

- Org sections: `organizations/detail/organization-section-frame.tsx`
- Branch: `branch-detail-view.tsx` + `branch-detail-hero.tsx`
- Court: `courts/detail/court-overview-view.tsx`
- Branch secondary tabs: `branches/detail/branch-tab-state.tsx` (`BranchTabBody`)
- Pricing detail: `pricing-profiles/pricing-profile-detail.tsx`

